     "senderName": "NWS Pueblo CO",
     "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 25 at 11:43PM MDT until October 27 at 12:45AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
     "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1245 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1141 PM MDT, Gauge reports indicated high stream flows.\nFlooding is already occurring in the warned area.\n- Widespread inundation of agriculture fields, wetlands, and other\nlow-lying areas.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
     "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
