     "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 25 at 10:47PM MDT until October 26 at 1:15AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
     "description": "* WHAT...Flooding continues, especially along the Conejos River\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Conejos County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 115 AM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will continue across low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations, especially along and near the Conejos River.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1047 PM MDT, River gauge reports indicate elevated river\nlevels continue due to multiple days of heavy rainfall. The\nConejos River at Mogote has crested, although high flows and\nflooding will persist, especially downstream from Mogote to the\nconfluence with the Rio Grande.\n- Some locations that may experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford and Conejos.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
